report=f"""# READY-COVER report\n\nStatus: **LOCALLY_CHECKED_BOUNDED_COVERAGE; coordinator re-review required**. This run does not build or approve a RAG, database, model, server deployment or site procedure.\n\nThe matrix contains {len(domain_rows)} domains, {len(tasks)} tasks, {len(decisions)} source decisions, {len(file_bindings)} exact-file source-use bindings, {len(supp)} supplement records and {len(open_items)} open items. Claims now point to exact content/fact/protocol locators. SRC-041 and SRC-042 have no frozen original and are excluded from content support. SRC-043 is excluded from product operating-limit support.\n\nFoundational coverage now distinguishes electrical energy, heat and temperature, calorimetry assumptions, battery electrochemical orientation, and capacity/SOC/SOH boundaries. Measurement coverage includes dataset readers/contracts and NIST uncertainty/reporting principles. It does not claim sensor calibration, a universal SOH estimator, causal failure diagnosis or production-tool validation.\n\nSource-use decisions separate historical registry statements from this run's exact-file actions and rights records for all 300 frozen originals. SRC-017 records 150 current prepared originals rather than repeating the older catalog-only statement; SRC-009 is resolved per file rather than by directory label. Open-licensed content and bounded local preparation are separated. OpenStax pages remain human/reference-only because of their explicit generative-AI restriction. Required heat/temperature/calorimetry support instead uses the public-release DOE fundamentals handbook; that historical handbook is not treated as a current operating standard.\n\nRemaining items are case/site inputs, conditional rule access, dataset-specific semantic limits, and the future AI-use split. Air transport still needs current commercial DGR/carrier rules when selected.\n\nExecuted validation command is recorded in `CHECK_RESULTS.json`; it checks selector resolution, semantic guardrails, row counts, supplement hashes and the root round-1 findings. It does not validate scientific fitness for every future case or downstream model behavior.\n"""
